msgid "<action>Toggle</action> the Statusbar"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: using-kturtle.docbook:483
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Settings</guimenu> <guisubmenu>Advanced Settings</guisubmenu>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: using-kturtle.docbook:487
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Here you can change things you normally do not need to change. The "
"<guisubmenu>Advanced Settings</guisubmenu> submenu has three items: "
"<guimenuitem>Configure Editor...</guimenuitem> (the standard &kate; editor "
"settings dialog), <guimenuitem>Configure Shortcuts...</guimenuitem> (the "
"standard &kde; shortcut settings dialog), and <guimenuitem>Configure "
"Toolbars...</guimenuitem> (the standard &kde; toolbars setting dialog)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: using-kturtle.docbook:493
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guimenu>Settings</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Configure &kturtle;...</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: using-kturtle.docbook:497
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This is used to configure &kturtle;. Here you can change the language of the "
"&logo; commands or set a new initial canvas size."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: using-kturtle.docbook:504
#, no-c-format
msgid "The <guimenu>Help</guimenu> Menu"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: using-kturtle.docbook:508
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut> <keycombo><keysym>F1</keysym></keycombo> </shortcut> "
"<guimenu>Help</guimenu> <guimenuitem>&kturtle; Handbook</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: using-kturtle.docbook:515
#, no-c-format
msgid "This action shows the handbook that you are currently reading."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: using-kturtle.docbook:521
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut> <keycombo>&Shift;<keysym>F1</keysym></keycombo> </shortcut> "
"<guimenu>Help</guimenu> <guimenuitem>What's This?</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: using-kturtle.docbook:528
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"After activating this action the mouse arrow will be changed into a "
"<quote>question mark arrow</quote>. When this arrow is used to click on "
"parts of &kturtle; main window, a description of the particular part pops-up."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: using-kturtle.docbook:534
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<shortcut> <keycombo><keysym>F2</keysym></keycombo> </shortcut> "
"<guimenu>Help</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Help on: ...</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: using-kturtle.docbook:541
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This is a very useful function: it provides help on the code where the "
"cursor in the code editor is at. So, &eg;, you have used the "
"<userinput>print</userinput> command in your code, and you want to read and "
"to know what the handbook says on this command. You just move your cursor so "
"it is in the <userinput>print</userinput> command and you press <keysym>F2</"
"keysym>. The handbook will then show all info on the <userinput>print</"
"userinput> command."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: using-kturtle.docbook:542
#, no-c-format
msgid "This function is very important while learning programming."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: using-kturtle.docbook:548
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Help</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Report Bug...</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: using-kturtle.docbook:552
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Use this to report a problem with &kturtle; to the developers. These reports "
"can be used to make future versions of &kturtle; even better."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: using-kturtle.docbook:558
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Help</guimenu> <guimenuitem>About &kturtle;</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: using-kturtle.docbook:562
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Here you find information on &kturtle;, like the authors and the license it "
"comes with."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: using-kturtle.docbook:568
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>Help</guimenu> <guimenuitem>About &kde;</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: using-kturtle.docbook:572
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Here you can find information on &kde;. If you do not know yet what &kde; "
"is, this is a place you should not miss."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: using-kturtle.docbook:580
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Toolbar"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: using-kturtle.docbook:581
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Here you can quickly reach the most used actions. By default, you will find "
"here all main useful commands ending with the <guiicon>Execute Commands</"
"guiicon> and <guiicon>Stop Execution</guiicon> icons."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: using-kturtle.docbook:582
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can configure the toolbar using <menuchoice><guimenu>Settings</"
"guimenu><guimenuitem>Advanced Settings</guimenuitem><guimenuitem>Configure "
"Toolbars...</guimenuitem></menuchoice>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: using-kturtle.docbook:586
#, no-c-format
msgid "The Statusbar"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: using-kturtle.docbook:587
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"On the status bar you get feedback of the state of &kturtle;. On the left "
"side it shows the feedback on the last action. On the right side you find "
"the current location of the cursor (line and column numbers). In the middle "
"of the Status bar is indicated the current language used for the commands."
msgstr ""
